The Last Train Heist — 35 s recut — a Tilt-Shift Miniature short for Pocket City (YouTube Shorts, 1080×1920), from the user's own script

Picture
- Everything is procedural three.js code in this folder (the toy map, viaduct, station, tunnel, apartment blocks, fire escape, bank, café, thief, police cars, helicopter, civilian traffic, train, billboard, street sweeper in scene.js, actors.js and kit.js). No image assets, no footage, no image or video generator.
- Post-processing adapted from an MIT-licensed tilt-shift pass (post.js); geometry helper geo.js (MIT).

Voice
- None (a wordless film).

Music
- None (the script asks for 100% sound effects).

Sound effects
- All synthesized in mix.py (no recorded samples).

Software
- three.js (MIT), playwright-core (Apache-2.0), FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL), numpy/scipy (BSD), soundfile (BSD)
